WEBVTT

00:00:16.750 --> 00:00:19.708
A-A back attack at point-blank range?

00:00:19.708 --> 00:00:22.750
It came so suddenly--and out of nowhere!

00:00:22.750 --> 00:00:25.167
There wasn't anyone there until just now!

00:00:27.417 --> 00:00:29.417
I get it...

00:00:29.417 --> 00:00:32.500
So he was blending in with Mr. Karasuma?

00:00:32.500 --> 00:00:35.792
The only one to use Self-Defense Force camo--

00:00:35.792 --> 00:00:39.292
and he waited for his prey
at the perfect sniping point!

00:00:41.542 --> 00:00:43.500
Gotcha!

00:00:47.875 --> 00:00:49.000
"Blue: Hiroto Maehara"
"Dead"

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:53.208
That's why I get so antsy--
because he pulls stunts like that.

00:00:53.208 --> 00:00:55.500
Now we're one-on-one...

00:00:55.500 --> 00:00:58.583
Let's finish this, Nagisa.

00:01:04.500 --> 00:01:06.917
<i>"Wait, just hang on a sec!"</i>

00:01:06.917 --> 00:01:09.958
<i>I scream, but it gets me nowhere</i>

00:01:09.958 --> 00:01:12.417
<i>I put all my strength into being afraid of</i>

00:01:12.417 --> 00:01:15.208
<i>The limits that just kept on closing in</i>

00:01:15.208 --> 00:01:17.750
<i>Reality is merciless</i>

00:01:17.750 --> 00:01:20.458
<i>And time is especially tricky</i>

00:01:20.458 --> 00:01:25.708
<i>It's like someone's snatching away</i>
<i>the blanket I just can't sleep without</i>

00:01:25.708 --> 00:01:31.792
<i>We laughed and fretted</i>

00:01:31.792 --> 00:01:36.333
<i>Over silly things, nonsensical things</i>

00:01:36.333 --> 00:01:42.458
<i>Once the final bell rings out</i>

00:01:42.458 --> 00:01:47.042
<i>The fun times will be over, too</i>

00:01:47.042 --> 00:01:48.583
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:01:48.583 --> 00:01:54.625
<i>365 days' worth of lessons shoved into bags</i>

00:01:54.625 --> 00:01:57.708
<i>Like always, like it's "see you tomorrow"</i>

00:01:57.708 --> 00:01:59.250
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:01:59.250 --> 00:02:03.333
<i>365 days' worth of happenings</i>

00:02:03.333 --> 00:02:08.333
<i>If you've made me an adult,</i>
<i>don't be showing me tears</i>

00:02:08.333 --> 00:02:09.833
<i>Bye-bye, yesterday</i>

00:02:09.833 --> 00:02:11.292
<i>365 days' worth of memories</i>

00:02:11.292 --> 00:02:13.917
"64 Days Till Koro Sensei's Dead-Line"
<i>365 days' worth of memories</i>

00:02:13.917 --> 00:02:16.417
<i>Even if I grow up some more</i>

00:02:16.417 --> 00:02:19.250
<i>They still won't fade a bit</i>

00:02:29.042 --> 00:02:33.083
"18th Period: Outcome Time"
"by Sosuke Sugaya"

00:02:40.625 --> 00:02:44.000
So now it's down to Nagisa and Karma.

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:48.917
Pretty gutsy of Nagisa
to hide behind Karasuma like that.

00:02:48.917 --> 00:02:52.667
The referee has the least
presence in the players' vision.

00:02:52.667 --> 00:02:56.042
Nagisa zeroed in on that,
blended in with the referee--

00:02:56.042 --> 00:03:00.458
<i>and </i>waited until the moment
he could score the most kills.

00:03:00.458 --> 00:03:03.500
He has the sense of a natural-born killer!

00:03:04.250 --> 00:03:07.500
And what about Karma?

00:03:07.500 --> 00:03:10.292
Comparing them on regular school grades,

00:03:10.292 --> 00:03:14.250
he's got Nagisa beat on all counts.

00:03:14.250 --> 00:03:17.833
But he must have realized by now:

00:03:17.833 --> 00:03:20.458
When it comes to enemies
in this assassination classroom,

00:03:20.458 --> 00:03:25.375
Karma's greatest foe is Nagisa.

00:03:28.625 --> 00:03:31.542
He's moved already?

00:03:31.542 --> 00:03:35.583
Nagisa! Put down the gun and come on out!

00:03:35.583 --> 00:03:38.417
We'll settle it with these!

00:03:38.417 --> 00:03:42.583
Nagisa, you dummy! Shoot him!
He's walking toward you wide open!

00:03:42.583 --> 00:03:44.875
I... don't think he'll shoot.

00:03:44.875 --> 00:03:46.750
Huh?

00:03:46.750 --> 00:03:49.167
That Karma...

00:03:49.167 --> 00:03:51.958
He sure plays dirty.

00:03:51.958 --> 00:03:54.917
If I ignore the challenge
and shoot him with no provocation,

00:03:54.917 --> 00:03:58.833
the red team'll be hard-pressed
to accept the way they lost.

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:02.042
And he knows it, too.

00:04:04.417 --> 00:04:09.833
If I want everyone to be
in agreement on saving Koro Sensei,

00:04:09.833 --> 00:04:14.333
I have no choice but to take him on
in close combat--his specialty.

00:04:14.333 --> 00:04:15.375
Nagisa!

00:04:15.375 --> 00:04:17.542
They're going <i>mano a mano</i>?! No way!

00:04:17.542 --> 00:04:20.792
Nagisa wants Karma,
more than anyone else, to understand

00:04:20.792 --> 00:04:23.375
his desire to save Koro Sensei.

00:04:23.375 --> 00:04:25.625
Let's watch from closer in!

00:04:28.125 --> 00:04:32.625
It's like... I still don't want to kill him,

00:04:32.625 --> 00:04:35.833
but taking on a tough opponent
with a lot of resolve, well...

00:04:35.833 --> 00:04:40.583
My hands still have that feeling
of accomplishment from killing Rinka.

00:04:40.583 --> 00:04:45.792
Will I feel like this
after we kill Koro Sensei, too?

00:04:45.792 --> 00:04:49.292
Here come the wavering opinions.

00:04:49.292 --> 00:04:54.167
Guess we change our tune
once the camo stops working, eh?

00:04:54.167 --> 00:04:57.292
Some of us showed
a strength we didn't expect,

00:04:57.292 --> 00:05:00.917
like you and Kayano and Mimura and Kanzaki.

00:05:00.917 --> 00:05:04.750
And some of us went ballistic
like we thought they would,

00:05:04.750 --> 00:05:07.500
some got all fired up to do better next time,

00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:10.625
and some irresponsible-lookin' types
turned out to be crazy serious.

00:05:10.625 --> 00:05:11.708
Hush, you.

00:05:11.708 --> 00:05:16.125
The guy we thought was just a little runt
turned out to be a genius assassin,

00:05:16.125 --> 00:05:21.417
and a guy we thought was a genius
was secretly workin' hard all along.

00:05:21.417 --> 00:05:24.458
Whichever of 'em wins is fine by me.

00:05:24.458 --> 00:05:27.250
With all these different skillsets...

00:05:27.250 --> 00:05:31.208
...we just might be able to handle
any challenge that comes our way.

00:05:38.375 --> 00:05:41.417
Ever since first year...

00:05:41.417 --> 00:05:44.125
To put it simply, I looked up to Karma.

00:05:45.000 --> 00:05:48.000
Hey, sir, what's this here?

00:05:48.000 --> 00:05:51.667
Ah, Akabane! Moving into
second-year territory already?

00:05:51.667 --> 00:05:54.250
He did what he wanted
and was completely unafraid.

00:05:54.250 --> 00:05:56.417
And yet, he was smart and could do anything.

00:05:56.417 --> 00:06:01.458
Okay, that's all I was
wondering about. I've got the rest.

00:06:01.458 --> 00:06:03.500
Hey, Akabane!

00:06:03.500 --> 00:06:05.000
I'm leaving early--I'm thirsty.

00:06:05.000 --> 00:06:06.833
"ZStudy Support" "Mathematics: Algebra"
I'm leaving early--I'm thirsty.

00:06:06.833 --> 00:06:10.292
If only I could be like that...

00:06:10.292 --> 00:06:13.583
That's how I felt, in my ordinariness.

00:06:13.583 --> 00:06:14.542
"Movie Plaza" "Premiering Soon! Sonic Ninja" "Full Coverage Inside!"

00:06:14.542 --> 00:06:16.083
"Movie Plaza" "Premiering Soon! Sonic Ninja" "Full Coverage Inside!"
Whoa, no way!

00:06:16.083 --> 00:06:20.250
Nazzoni directed Sonic Ninja?
How cool is that?

00:06:20.250 --> 00:06:25.833
Ooh, and it opens today? Let's go, Shiota!

00:06:25.833 --> 00:06:29.167
Uh, yeah!

00:06:29.167 --> 00:06:35.708
So I was happy when he talked to me,
and we started to hang out.

00:06:35.708 --> 00:06:38.125
That was halfway through our first year.

00:06:39.208 --> 00:06:44.167
But we couldn't stay friends for long.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:49.833
You Karma? You got nerve,
beatin' up a guy's pal like that!

00:06:49.833 --> 00:06:54.792
Huh? News to me. Besides, he started it.

00:06:54.792 --> 00:06:57.375
Bullshit! He told me that--

00:07:03.083 --> 00:07:06.708
Can't hear you! What was that? Say it again!

00:07:06.708 --> 00:07:08.708
--Come on!
--He could stand where he did

00:07:08.708 --> 00:07:11.708
because he had the strength
to win in studying and fighting both.

00:07:13.083 --> 00:07:16.083
His was a stage I could never hope to share.

00:07:16.083 --> 00:07:16.417
"ZStudy Support" "Mathematics: Algebra"
His was a stage I could never hope to share.

00:07:16.417 --> 00:07:20.958
"ZStudy Support" "Mathematics: Algebra"
He must have gotten bored, being on my stage with me.

00:07:20.958 --> 00:07:23.500
By the time he had gotten suspended,

00:07:23.500 --> 00:07:26.542
we'd gone back to being plain old classmates.

00:07:27.875 --> 00:07:30.750
He's a harmless little mouse,

00:07:30.750 --> 00:07:33.042
making him one of the few people
a combative guy like me

00:07:33.042 --> 00:07:36.458
didn't have to be careful around.

00:07:36.458 --> 00:07:41.708
But looking back,
I put that distance between us...

00:07:41.708 --> 00:07:45.917
...because there was already a part
of him back then that made me uneasy.

00:07:48.167 --> 00:07:53.250
Huh? Where'd he go? Nagisa!

00:07:53.250 --> 00:07:56.083
I could put my guard down around him...

00:07:59.167 --> 00:08:03.792
I'm right here, Karma. Didn't you see me?

00:08:03.792 --> 00:08:06.708
...but something kept me on alert.

00:08:06.708 --> 00:08:10.500
Something that could
kill me in my sleep one day.

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:13.458
--Sorry 'bout that, Nagisa! You're just so small!
--He was so honest and good, unlike me,

00:08:13.458 --> 00:08:14.292
--Ugh.
--He was so honest and good, unlike me,

00:08:14.292 --> 00:08:17.708
that my anxiety had to be all in my head.

00:08:17.708 --> 00:08:21.708
Still, he had this mysterious... <i>something</i>

00:08:21.708 --> 00:08:25.375
that I wanted to drag out of him and crush.

00:08:25.375 --> 00:08:27.375
And <i>that </i>part is scary.

00:08:27.375 --> 00:08:31.708
But there's no point in
beating him in fights and in class.

00:08:31.708 --> 00:08:35.667
This whatever-it-is is
something else altogether.

00:08:36.542 --> 00:08:40.917
It was hard to handle, and before
I knew it, we had drifted apart.

00:08:40.917 --> 00:08:48.208
Now for the first time, in year 3,
we're up on the same stage: assassination!

00:08:48.208 --> 00:08:52.792
And we need to win
to get our own points across!

00:08:53.958 --> 00:08:55.875
You're going down!

00:08:56.083 --> 00:09:00.083
"Assassination Classroom, Final Season"
"by Nagisa Shiota"

00:09:08.542 --> 00:09:10.208
Nagisa...

00:09:10.208 --> 00:09:13.208
A desire to win, to conquer--

00:09:13.208 --> 00:09:16.708
the great competitive spirit
permitted in the young!

00:09:16.708 --> 00:09:20.042
You must forget all about me!

00:09:20.042 --> 00:09:24.292
Your own answer is there before you!

00:09:31.000 --> 00:09:31.958
Kill!

00:09:31.958 --> 00:09:33.667
Save!

00:09:50.708 --> 00:09:53.708
A tackle with that timing
won't bring him down?

00:09:53.708 --> 00:09:56.458
There <i>is </i>a huge
power difference between them.

00:09:56.458 --> 00:09:59.792
Yes: if one knife connects, it's a win,

00:09:59.792 --> 00:10:02.542
but Karma's active skills will use
the lead-up to that moment

00:10:02.542 --> 00:10:04.750
to his advantage.

00:10:04.750 --> 00:10:07.583
Now, look at Nagisa.

00:10:07.583 --> 00:10:11.250
He has another knife!

00:10:11.250 --> 00:10:13.958
In preparation for a clap stunner?

00:10:13.958 --> 00:10:17.458
But Karma will have noticed, of course.

00:10:17.458 --> 00:10:20.708
It won't be easy to use it against him.

00:10:20.708 --> 00:10:24.333
Two assassins, their weapons
and approaches worlds apart:

00:10:24.333 --> 00:10:26.750
How will they settle this?

00:10:26.750 --> 00:10:29.333
Stay tuned!

00:10:43.000 --> 00:10:47.292
If I take these blows wrong,
I'll be inked for sure.

00:10:53.625 --> 00:10:54.875
Now!

00:10:54.875 --> 00:10:56.292
Tch!

00:10:56.958 --> 00:10:59.208
Nice! He took his knife away!

00:10:59.208 --> 00:11:00.625
Now's my chance!

00:11:03.542 --> 00:11:05.125
They <i>both </i>dropped their weapons?

00:11:05.125 --> 00:11:07.750
But Nagisa has another one!

00:11:13.042 --> 00:11:14.917
I'm not letting you draw it.

00:11:14.917 --> 00:11:17.500
The second you try, I'll hit you.

00:11:17.500 --> 00:11:21.458
I'll knock you out, then take
my sweet time dealing the final blow!

00:11:31.333 --> 00:11:33.208
That all you got?

00:11:38.125 --> 00:11:41.750
Karma's taking Nagisa's attacks on purpose.

00:11:41.750 --> 00:11:47.417
His hits <i>have </i>to be doing <i>something</i>.
He's been training a whole year!

00:11:47.417 --> 00:11:51.208
Karma is a combat assassin
who values the process.

00:11:51.208 --> 00:11:54.542
Bargaining, strategy,
how to defeat your foe...

00:11:54.542 --> 00:11:57.958
...and after <i>that </i>battle
comes his assassination.

00:11:57.958 --> 00:12:00.792
Nagisa, on the other hand, is a pure assassin,

00:12:00.792 --> 00:12:04.208
singlemindedly searching for
the one strike that will lead to victory.

00:12:04.208 --> 00:12:09.375
And Karma takes it all, blow after blow.

00:12:09.375 --> 00:12:14.542
If he wins like that,
even Nagisa will have to accept defeat.

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:27.625
An axe kick!

00:12:27.625 --> 00:12:31.292
Bring that to a fight and
the other guy doesn't stand a chance!

00:12:39.583 --> 00:12:45.083
I'll probably never find
another place like this again,

00:12:45.083 --> 00:12:48.667
where your feelings can be
right out in the open.

00:12:50.542 --> 00:12:52.750
But I <i>will </i>kill him...

00:12:52.750 --> 00:12:56.458
...because I believe it's right.

00:13:05.292 --> 00:13:08.083
What--now?!

00:13:08.083 --> 00:13:10.667
That's the last of his strength!

00:13:10.667 --> 00:13:13.208
He bit his tongue to keep from going down!

00:13:13.208 --> 00:13:15.792
Just you try killing me, Nagisa...

00:13:15.792 --> 00:13:18.750
...with that talent I never had!

00:13:18.750 --> 00:13:21.958
I'll break it all right over my knee--

00:13:21.958 --> 00:13:24.750
and win!

00:13:24.750 --> 00:13:27.333
All that bloodlust, condensed into that knife.

00:13:27.333 --> 00:13:30.708
If I can just dodge that, I win!

00:13:31.500 --> 00:13:32.958
Huh?

00:13:32.958 --> 00:13:35.750
N-No bloodlust?!

00:13:38.375 --> 00:13:40.125
An arm-triangle choke?!

00:13:40.125 --> 00:13:43.542
That arm pressing on his carotid
will make him pass out!

00:13:43.542 --> 00:13:47.125
It's an even more perfect position
than his earlier triangle choke!

00:13:49.208 --> 00:13:51.792
You <i>will </i>hear me out!

00:13:51.792 --> 00:13:55.792
How is he pinning
Karma down so awesomely?!

00:13:55.792 --> 00:14:00.125
Nagisa used his own
best assassination skill as a sacrifice

00:14:00.125 --> 00:14:02.708
and chose martial arts for his finisher.

00:14:02.708 --> 00:14:08.625
All so he could end things
using Karma's specialty, not his.

00:14:08.625 --> 00:14:15.750
Just like I did to Nagisa--he's trying
to get me to accept my defeat.

00:14:15.750 --> 00:14:17.542
Uh-oh.

00:14:17.542 --> 00:14:19.625
At this rate...

00:14:19.625 --> 00:14:21.583
...I'll be toast!

00:14:27.250 --> 00:14:28.083
A knife!

00:14:28.083 --> 00:14:30.625
That close?

00:14:36.333 --> 00:14:38.417
Me, fight?

00:14:38.417 --> 00:14:41.500
I think I'd be too scared to fight.

00:14:41.500 --> 00:14:45.208
I mean, if my life depended on it...

00:14:48.250 --> 00:14:51.167
Uncle. I give.

00:14:51.167 --> 00:14:54.208
I lost, Nagisa.

00:14:55.917 --> 00:14:57.167
Hey! Listen!

00:14:57.167 --> 00:14:59.000
That's enough!

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:00.833
Due to the red team's surrender,

00:15:00.833 --> 00:15:03.833
the blue team--the "don't kill" team--has won!

00:15:03.833 --> 00:15:06.500
Yesss!

00:15:06.500 --> 00:15:10.875
Aw... Well, you won, Nagisa.

00:15:12.292 --> 00:15:16.542
I won? I... beat Karma?

00:15:16.542 --> 00:15:20.458
Like anyone would
approve of me using a knife

00:15:20.458 --> 00:15:25.792
to beat a barehanded mouse
who showed that much moxie.

00:15:25.792 --> 00:15:28.708
I couldn't stab you, and I couldn't get away.

00:15:28.708 --> 00:15:32.333
I was backed into a corner,
where all I could do was surrender.

00:15:32.333 --> 00:15:35.958
You beat me with martial arts,
not with a knife.

00:15:35.958 --> 00:15:40.208
To think that was the best way to kill me...

00:15:41.292 --> 00:15:47.667
I got slaughtered. You want
to save Koro Sensei? I'm listening.

00:15:48.833 --> 00:15:51.292
Really? Are you sure?

00:15:51.292 --> 00:15:54.458
Don't give me that dumb look
with that beat-up face of yours.

00:15:54.458 --> 00:15:57.375
You look like a plague rat.

00:15:57.375 --> 00:16:03.708
Th-Those insults sure do
trip right off your tongue, Karma...

00:16:03.708 --> 00:16:04.917
Look...

00:16:04.917 --> 00:16:06.917
Hup!

00:16:06.917 --> 00:16:10.375
...why don't we drop the formality already?

00:16:10.375 --> 00:16:13.417
I don't much feel like
sticking with it after that fight.

00:16:13.417 --> 00:16:16.625
What, <i>now</i>?

00:16:16.625 --> 00:16:19.583
It feels weird to change this late in the game.

00:16:19.583 --> 00:16:26.042
I'll do it, then. Okay, Nagisa?

00:16:28.667 --> 00:16:31.625
All right, Karma.

00:16:35.917 --> 00:16:40.333
When a big decision looms,
people reveal their true feelings--

00:16:40.333 --> 00:16:43.167
and, in some cases, fight in earnest.

00:16:43.167 --> 00:16:46.167
But take a look at these students.

00:16:46.167 --> 00:16:48.958
It's precisely because
they all fought in earnest

00:16:48.958 --> 00:16:54.625
that they can understand what
they normally don't show one another.

00:16:54.625 --> 00:16:59.875
Sometimes conflict can be the best
opportunity to deepen friendships.

00:16:59.875 --> 00:17:01.625
How would you put it?

00:17:01.625 --> 00:17:05.042
"Discord and conflict
are part of education, too"?

00:17:08.875 --> 00:17:11.625
I'm sure you all
have your own thoughts on this.

00:17:11.625 --> 00:17:15.292
I have no objection to
the course the class has chosen.

00:17:15.292 --> 00:17:19.667
However, there's one condition
on your search for a way to save him:

00:17:19.667 --> 00:17:23.208
You have until the end of the month.

00:17:23.208 --> 00:17:25.917
Though you might be
taking a break from assassination,

00:17:25.917 --> 00:17:30.292
there are plenty of other efforts
underway to take this guy down.

00:17:30.292 --> 00:17:33.000
If someone's going to kill him,
it can't be anyone else.

00:17:33.000 --> 00:17:35.917
I want it to be you.

00:17:35.917 --> 00:17:39.958
So promise me that
no matter how January turns out,

00:17:39.958 --> 00:17:44.292
February and beyond will be spent
giving your all to assassination.

00:17:44.292 --> 00:17:48.208
Whether you save him
or kill him... give it your all.

00:17:50.208 --> 00:17:51.667
Yes, sir!

00:17:52.833 --> 00:18:04.833
<i>In the big window where</i>
<i>the dappled sunlight shines gently in</i>

00:18:04.833 --> 00:18:16.792
<i>The day I met you felt so far away</i>

00:18:16.792 --> 00:18:27.708
<i>The memories I've arranged</i>
<i>little by little keep me warm</i>

00:18:27.708 --> 00:18:39.292
<i>A small room, hearts connecting:</i>
<i>you taught me gently</i>

00:18:39.292 --> 00:18:52.042
<i>Once this season comes for me, I won't be able</i>

00:18:52.042 --> 00:18:57.292
<i>To search out your figure anymore</i>

00:18:57.292 --> 00:19:03.000
<i>I'll never forget</i>

00:19:03.000 --> 00:19:09.583
<i>Until the day I can see you again</i>

00:19:23.292 --> 00:19:25.458
Let's think about this in general terms.

00:19:25.458 --> 00:19:30.667
Are the world's leaders really
<i>only </i>thinking about killing Koro Sensei?

00:19:30.667 --> 00:19:32.542
I don't think so.

00:19:32.542 --> 00:19:36.625
After all, their original goal is to save Earth.

00:19:36.625 --> 00:19:38.500
Along with their research on killing him,

00:19:38.500 --> 00:19:41.500
they must be doing research
that doesn't involve killing him, too.

00:19:41.500 --> 00:19:44.417
Why don't we look into that?

00:19:44.417 --> 00:19:47.333
It's true: the world's top science facilities

00:19:47.333 --> 00:19:50.667
have formed project teams focused on saving the planet.

00:19:50.667 --> 00:19:50.958
"Tentacle"
have formed project teams focused on saving the planet.

00:19:50.958 --> 00:19:54.042
"Tentacle"
Naturally, that info is all top-secret.

00:19:54.042 --> 00:19:56.458
It would be tough for you
to find out what they're studying.

00:19:56.458 --> 00:19:58.958
I've infiltrated the project database!

00:19:58.958 --> 00:20:00.125
<i>What</i>?!

00:20:00.125 --> 00:20:04.167
I can get into just about any online PC.

00:20:04.167 --> 00:20:07.625
I've learned so much this year!

00:20:07.625 --> 00:20:09.250
Ritsu...

00:20:09.250 --> 00:20:12.125
Wow! We can see what labs
around the world are researching

00:20:12.125 --> 00:20:14.250
and on what schedule!

00:20:14.250 --> 00:20:20.208
But there are no online traces
of the data we're looking for.

00:20:20.208 --> 00:20:23.833
I guess the top-secret stuff
is only passed around in person.

00:20:23.833 --> 00:20:27.625
Is anyone doing research on
how to save Koro Sensei, then?

00:20:27.625 --> 00:20:30.375
There! An American research team!

00:20:30.375 --> 00:20:33.500
"Preventing destructive
antimatter chain reactions

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:39.000
due to tentacle-cell aging and fission"!

00:20:39.000 --> 00:20:44.792
"Final samples to be returned
from ISS on 1/25"...?

00:20:44.792 --> 00:20:47.083
ISS--is that...

00:20:47.083 --> 00:20:50.500
Th-The International Space Station?!

00:20:50.500 --> 00:20:53.042
<i>That's </i>where they're doing their research?!

00:20:53.042 --> 00:20:55.250
Oh! It could be!

00:20:55.250 --> 00:20:59.333
Lots of research has to be done
in zero gravity or in a vacuum.

00:20:59.333 --> 00:21:04.292
And if there's any chance an experiment
could cause a huge explosion...

00:21:04.292 --> 00:21:06.708
...there'd be less damage in outer space!

00:21:06.708 --> 00:21:09.250
If we could only see that data...

00:21:09.250 --> 00:21:14.000
Unfortunately, you're just one tiny,
distant outpost of assassins.

00:21:14.000 --> 00:21:18.125
Depending on the circumstances,
that data may never come.

00:21:21.708 --> 00:21:23.542
Mr. Karasuma?

00:21:24.583 --> 00:21:26.375
No matter what happens,

00:21:26.375 --> 00:21:28.750
we won't quit this assassination.

00:21:28.750 --> 00:21:32.083
But we don't want to be lukewarm about it.

00:21:32.083 --> 00:21:35.375
If there's a way to save him, we will.

00:21:35.375 --> 00:21:38.708
And if not...
we've decided to handle that, too.

00:21:38.708 --> 00:21:40.375
Right, Nagisa?

00:21:40.375 --> 00:21:44.417
Right. After all,
it's our class's critical goal.

00:21:44.417 --> 00:21:47.167
So I want to know for sure, right now--

00:21:47.167 --> 00:21:52.458
so we can stick with
our assassination till we graduate.

00:21:52.458 --> 00:21:58.292
Mr. Karasuma, Miss Irina,
could you please step out?

00:21:59.292 --> 00:22:04.667
This chat could potentially
cause liability issues for you two.

00:22:05.792 --> 00:22:07.167
Now then...

00:22:07.167 --> 00:22:09.708
Here's what you're trying to do:

00:22:09.708 --> 00:22:12.792
sneak a peek at the data
before it reaches America

00:22:12.792 --> 00:22:15.667
on its way back from space.

00:22:15.667 --> 00:22:17.833
But how...

00:22:17.833 --> 00:22:19.958
About that!

00:22:20.708 --> 00:22:21.000
"Photo: Proof-of-Concept Craft Under Development" "Show All"

00:22:21.000 --> 00:22:26.208
"Photo: Proof-of-Concept Craft Under Development" "Show All"
Did you know they're about to send this baby up to the ISS?

00:22:26.208 --> 00:22:28.083
A manned rocket?

00:22:28.083 --> 00:22:32.125
Yes--a proof-of-concept craft
being developed here in Japan.

00:22:32.125 --> 00:22:35.792
It's supposed to carry
an experimental dummy, but...

00:22:35.792 --> 00:22:39.708
...what if there were real people in it instead?

00:22:40.500 --> 00:22:41.625
You don't mean--

00:22:41.625 --> 00:22:45.583
Ha! Our teacher's crazy in the head, all right.

00:22:45.583 --> 00:22:48.417
Yes! An out-of-season research project

00:22:48.417 --> 00:22:51.083
for our assassination classroom:

00:22:51.083 --> 00:22:55.833
Hijack the space station
and steal their experiment data!

00:22:55.833 --> 00:22:57.750
No way.

00:22:57.750 --> 00:23:01.184
<i>Yes</i>, way! <i>All </i>the way!
